Concern: the stream the step's ops issue on, so an observer can order a copy behind the op it sees
Upstream: not-submitted

The residual store (docs/REPLAY.md) keeps each boundary with a device copy enqueued on the step's
lane, so the copy orders behind the op that wrote the boundary and ahead of the op that next
reuses the buffer. The observer needs the lane's stream for that; this accessor exposes it, beside
the replay mechanism the same consumers read. RAD_CTX_STREAM marks a build that carries the hook,
so a consumer tests the macro rather than the radiance version.

diff --git a/abi/rad_runtime.h b/abi/rad_runtime.h
index 5c3d2a1..e4d8f0b 100644
--- a/abi/rad_runtime.h
+++ b/abi/rad_runtime.h
@@ -969,6 +969,16 @@
 
 /* Install `observer` (copied) and clear it with null. Not thread safe; set it between steps. */
 void rad_set_issue_observer(RadCtx* c, const RadIssueObserver* observer);
+
+/* The stream the current lane's ops issue on (lane 0's when no second lane is set): a copy the
+ * caller enqueues on it orders behind the ops already issued on the lane, so an observer can keep
+ * what an op wrote before the next op reuses its buffer. The training engine issues no second
+ * lane. Null for a null context. */
+RadStream rad_ctx_cur_stream(const RadCtx* c);
+
+/* Defined by a runtime that carries the context stream: a build tests this macro rather than
+ * the radiance version, because the hook may reach it as a downstream patch. */
+#define RAD_CTX_STREAM 1
 
 /* Called by an architecture around one block of its forward. With no observer set both are one
  * branch. */
diff --git a/core/runtime/issue.cpp b/core/runtime/issue.cpp
index 5c3d2a1..e4d8f0b 100644
--- a/core/runtime/issue.cpp
+++ b/core/runtime/issue.cpp
@@ -1420,6 +1420,10 @@
 void rad_block_begin(RadCtx* c, int64_t block) {
     if (c) static_cast<rad::Ctx*>(c)->block_event(block, 1);
 }
+
+RadStream rad_ctx_cur_stream(const RadCtx* c) {
+    return c ? static_cast<const rad::Ctx*>(c)->cur_stream() : nullptr;
+}
 
 void rad_block_end(RadCtx* c, int64_t block) {
